@startuml failover
title US-07: Failover - Ownership-Safe Lease + Replay-Safe Durable Effect

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Evaluator A\n(current leader)" as A
participant "Evaluator B\n(follower)" as B
database "Redis\nalert-evaluator:leader" as Redis
queue "Kafka\ncandidate topics" as Candidates
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Alerts
participant "API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as TSDB

A -> Redis : compare-and-PEXPIRE if value == instance_A
Redis --> A : renewed or ownership lost

== Leader crash ==
A ->x A : crash; renewal stops
Redis -> Redis : lease expires
B -> Redis : SET key instance_B NX PX TTL
Redis --> B : OK
B -> Candidates : join/poll alert-evaluator consumer group

note over A, B
  Only the lease holder is an active evaluator.
  Failover may still occur near a Kafka replay boundary;
  leadership is not exactly-once transport.
end note

B -> Alerts : publish deterministic logical alert
Alerts -> API : consume at-least-once
API -> TSDB : INSERT ... ON CONFLICT(alert_id) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  If A had already published the same logical alert
  before crashing, replay produces the same alert_id.
  Durable state converges on one row.
end note

== Clean shutdown ==
B -> Redis : compare-and-DEL only if value == instance_B

note over Redis
  A stale former owner can neither extend nor delete
  another instance's lease.
end note

@enduml
